---
title: Get Help
---
<!--=== Breadcrumbs ===-->
<div class="breadcrumbs margin-bottom-40">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="pull-left">Get Help</h1>
    <ul class="pull-right breadcrumb">
      <li><a href="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>">Home</a></li>
      <li class="active">Get Help</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div><!--/breadcrumbs-->
<!--=== End Breadcrumbs ===-->

<!--=== Content Part ===-->
<div class="container">
	<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-9">
      <p class="margin-bottom-20">
        Fluentd is maintained by its community. If you have a question or hit a problem, start with the channels below.
        They are all free to use, and answers come from other users and from maintainers when they have time.
      </p>

      <div class="clients-page margin-bottom-20">
        <img src="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>images/env_icon.png" alt="" />
        <p><h3><a href="https://github.com/fluent/fluentd/discussions">Forum</a></h3>
          Got a question? Have some cool Fluentd-related projects? The forum (GitHub Discussions) is the place to be.
          It is a good fit for how-to questions and for design discussions before you write a configuration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="clients-page margin-bottom-20">
        <img src="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>images/env_issue.png" alt="" />
        <p><h3><a href="https://github.com/fluent/fluentd/issues">Issue Tracker</a></h3>
          Do you think Fluentd has a bug? Do you wish Fluentd could do X? File an issue on GitHub.
          Please attach the steps to reproduce it, otherwise nobody can act on the report.
          Do not report a vulnerability here. See <a href="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>security">Security Advisories</a> for how to report it privately.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="clients-page margin-bottom-20">
        <img src="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>images/env_github.png" alt="" />
        <p><h3><a href="https://github.com/fluent/fluentd">Source Code</a></h3>
          Check out the source code. Contributions are always welcome.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="clients-page margin-bottom-20">
        <img src="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>images/env_slack.png" alt="" />
        <p><h3><a href="https://slack.cncf.io">Slack #fluentd</a></h3>
        Join our Slack channel!, register to get an invitation and stay in touch.
        Chat is good for a quick question, but it is not suitable to dig into the problem, so the forum is a better place for anything worth keeping.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="clients-page margin-bottom-20">
        <p>At the past, <a href="https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/fluentd">Mailing List</a> was used, but
          We migrated it to <a href="https://github.com/fluent/fluentd/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a> above, so please don't post new articles here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="headline margin-bottom-20"><h3>What to expect from community support</h3></div>
      <p>
        Knowing what the community can and cannot do saves you time when something is urgent.
      </p>
      <ul class="margin-bottom-20">
        <li>There is no guaranteed response time. Your question is answered when somebody has time for it.</li>
        <li>Maintainers decide what to work on and when, so you cannot raise the priority of your own issue or feature request.</li>
        <li>Whether a fix is backported to an older release depends on the support policy of that release. See <a href="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>download/fluent_package/releases">Fluent Package Maintenance Releases</a>.</li>
        <li>Nobody can look into your production environment, your configuration or your logs for you.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="headline margin-bottom-20"><h3>Commercial support</h3></div>
      <p class="margin-bottom-20">
        If you run Fluentd in production and need a guaranteed response time, help with your own environment,
        or a fix that lands on your own schedule, several companies offer commercial support for Fluentd.
        See <a href="<%= config[:http_prefix] %>enterprise_services">Enterprise Services</a> for the list.
      </p>

    </div><!--/col-md-9-->

    <div class="col-md-3">
      <%= partial "_right_menu" %>
    </div><!--/col-md-3-->
  </div><!--/row-->
</div><!--/container-->
<!--=== End Content Part ===-->
